<title>JAPAN: Japan Feb refined zinc output falls 0.3 percent.</title>
<headline>Japan Feb refined zinc output falls 0.3 percent.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese refined zinc output in February fell a seasonally adjusted 0.3 percent from the prior month, according to Ministry of International Trade and Industry data released on Friday.</p>
<p>On an unadjusted basis, output was off 8.1 percent year-on-year at 47,744 tonnes.</p>
<p>The February data was as follows (in tonnes, percent):</p>
<p>		 Feb 97     Jan 97   y/y change  s/a change*</p>
<p> Output	47,744     52,785     - 8.1	 - 0.3</p>
<p> Shipments   48,188     54,257     - 2.3	 -11.7</p>
<p> Stocks	54,180     54,260     -31.4	 - 0.8</p>
<p>(*Seasonally adjusted change, month-on-month)</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
